{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Do not say in your heart</b> — After He warned them not to think, \"My strength and the might of my hand has done this for me,\" but rather that they should know that HaShem gave them the power to prevail in war, and that the mightiest among them and the fortified cities which they would capture — HaShem in His glory did this for them through a public miracle from Him — He turned back and reminded them: do not think that HaShem did all this with you because of your righteousness, for He did not do this for you except because of the wickedness of these nations. Now, this is a reason for the destruction of those nations, but He did not give them a reason for Israel's inheritance of the land. Therefore He returned and explained: not by your righteousness — that you should be righteous in deed, nor even by an upright heart that you possessed — but rather because of the wickedness of the nations they were destroyed, and for the sake of the oath to your fathers you inherited that land. For your sin cannot nullify the gift that He gave to your fathers, because He gave it to them by oath. And Rashi wrote (Rashi on Deuteronomy 9:4): \"Do not say in your heart: my righteousness and the wickedness of the nations caused this for me — it is not by your righteousness.\" This is not correct. And the questioner may ask: behold, He said (Deuteronomy 7:8), \"Because of HaShem's love for you\" — and they are beloved on high, and HaShem loves only the good, for a wicked person and a lover of violence — His soul hates (Psalms 11:5). If so, they also inherited the land because of their righteousness. And the answer is that there He speaks with Israel in their entirety, whereas here He reproves that generation, who had been rebellious against HaShem from the day they were in the wilderness."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:47:13.609340634Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}